  "unmapped_findings": [
    "In the 15Al alloy, aging at 625 °C and 650 °C stabilizes the Vickers hardness between 800 HV and 900 HV with prolonged aging time; the 625 °C/6 h value (887.2 ± 14.1 HV) lies within this plateau (b0037).",
    "The optimal aging temperature range for achieving ultra-high hardness in the 15Al alloy is mainly 525 °C–600 °C, so the 625 °C aging condition lies above the optimal window for this alloy (b0038)."
